      "writtenOn": "2021-01-06T03:38:50Z",
      "side": 0,
      "message": "From RISC-V ISA Privileged Architecture (https://riscv.org/wp-content/uploads/2017/05/riscv-privileged-v1.10.pdf):\n\nMultiple simultaneous interrupts and traps at the same privilege level are handled in the following decreasing priority order: external interrupts, software interrupts, timer interrupts, then finally any synchronous traps.\n\n\nIf in_interrupt_context() \u003d\u003d true, it could be handling \"external interrupts\" or \"software interrupts\".  ebreak generates a new software interrupt which cannot preempt both of the cases.",
      "parentUuid": "c8a60974_35412829",
      "revId": "660672aa5427c1e33de000c47ecc5b9e31e89641",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
